# Screenshots are never versioned. They are captures of a real head unit in a
# real car, so they carry things no text search can find: a Wi-Fi SSID in the
# diagnostics NETWORK tile, map tiles around where the car actually parks, and
# whatever the cameras saw. One committed baseline
# (screenshots/flutter/07b_diagnostics_scrolled.png) did carry the SSID in
# plain text past a review, which is what retired this exception.
#
# native/ and flutter/ used to be versioned so a fresh clone had the parity
# baseline that gated deleting the native UI. That gate has been passed — the
# native UI is gone and the Flutter UI is verified on the device — so the
# reason for versioning them is spent.
#
# Captures are still useful locally; they just stay on the machine that took
# them. Anything that genuinely needs to ship gets redacted first (solid box
# over text, pixelate faces/plates — not blur, which can be undone) and added
# deliberately with `git add -f`.
screenshots/

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.beads-credential-key
# The ENTIRE Dolt backup directory — not just the chunks.
#
# This used to ignore only `.beads/backup/*.darc` and `oldgen/`, which left
# `manifest`, `backup_state.json` and `LOCK` tracked. That combination cannot work:
# `manifest` is Dolt's INDEX of which .darc chunks make up the backup, so git
# distributed an index for data git was refusing to carry. Any checkout that
# restored `manifest` pointed the backup at chunks that do not exist on this
# machine, and every `bd` command then failed with
#   auto-backup failed: ... error opening table file: table file not found
# Observed 2026-09-14 through 2026-09-16: the tracked manifest named 256 chunks
# while only 191 were present.
#
# A backup is a per-machine artifact and is regenerable with `bd backup sync`, so
# none of it belongs in source. Ignore the whole directory.
.beads/backup/

